  "title": "Risks and assumptions",
  "text": "The main risks involve document length, API development delays, and access to historical records during the migration gap [RSK-001, RSK-002, RSK-003]. We will enforce an 18-page limit, upload a baseline draft 24 hours prior to 2026-12-01 12:00 UTC, initiate a mock API environment, negotiate a phased go-live, prioritize frequently accessed records, and ensure staff retain read-only access to the legacy tool until migration completes [RSK-001, RSK-002, RSK-003]. This prevents outright proposal rejection, breaches of the go-live mandate, staff workflow disruption, and audit gaps [RSK-001, RSK-002, RSK-003]. Open questions remain regarding template forms, record formats, infrastructure, incident reporting channels, sandbox credentials, and migration data formats and volumes [Q-01, Q-02, Q-03, Q-04, Q-05, Q-06].",
